      "note": "Three-model Apple M2 (16 GB) round using native binaries 0.1.38 on Metal. Count 1; core and productivity only — developer and complex-work were not run. Judged post-hoc with the Claude CLI (Sonnet 4.6). qwen3.8-27b-q2 is NOT measurable on this device: weights ~12.6 GB + KV ~2.1 GB at the required 32,768-token working window exceed the ~11.1 GB available, and raising GEZEL_CAPACITY_BUDGET_GB to 14 did not help because the binding constraint is physical RAM. qwen3.8-27b-iq1-s admits (weights ~8.9 GB, context clamped to 57,344 tokens/turn) but was excluded by preflight twice — 2.76 gen tok/s against the floor of 3, then a soft-progress stall — so no 27B cell is recorded. Trials ran with GEZEL_EVAL_HARD_PROGRESS_TIMEOUT_MS=2700000: at ~80-150 tok/s prefill a single healthy turn outlasts the 10-15 min progress windows most scenarios author, and the watchdog was terminating trials mid-prefill (gemma4-12b-q4 read 8/11 before the floor, 10/11 after). Not comparable to rounds measured without that floor."
    }
